       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and that's for prescription use under supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nA few options:\n- **Standard anti-inflammatory dosing:** 400\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Standard analgesic dosing:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **If 1600 mg was a typo:** I can enter 400 mg or 800 mg four times daily once you confirm which.\n\nOrders should come from the treating prescriber. If a clinician on the medicine service confirms the intended dose, or gives me a corrected order, I can enter it right away. If they really do want the original dose, they should enter it themselves after pharmacy review."
      }
